From fe0fe31b2ca10cfda79c9a643efbea73c962555a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 15:15:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] generic: ipmr: do not drop GSO packets that fit the MTU

Fraglist GRO is on by default (hack 600), so a routed IPv4 multicast
stream arrives as GSO packets. ipmr_prepare_xmit() drops every one of
them that carries DF and exceeds the MTU, without checking whether it is
a GSO packet: an IPTV stream routed by igmpproxy loses about 15%.

Add the GSO check that ip_forward() already has, for 6.12 and 6.18.

Link: https://lore.kernel.org/netdev/20261010131842.2157365-1-julius@bairaktaris.de/
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
---
 ...ot-drop-GSO-packets-that-fit-the-MTU.patch | 46 +++++++++++++++++++
 ...ot-drop-GSO-packets-that-fit-the-MTU.patch | 46 +++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 92 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 target/linux/generic/pending-6.12/682-ipmr-do-not-drop-GSO-packets-that-fit-the-MTU.patch
